{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Topology Context Injection.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Topology Context Injection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"topology context injection topology context injection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Topology Context Injection.md","fileName":"Topology Context Injection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Topology Context Injection","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Network Copilot Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network Copilot Design","Network Knowledge Refresh","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Topology Context Injection.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Topology Context Injection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"topology context injection topology context injection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Topology Context Injection.md","fileName":"Topology Context Injection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Topology Context Injection","heading":"Topology Context Injection","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Topology context injection supplies a copilot with explicit device-to-device connections, interfaces, VLAN roles, subnets, and dependencies. It lets the assistant answer questions about where a port leads or what could be affected by a change instead of reasoning from isolated device facts.\n\nOnly the neighborhood needed for the question should enter the prompt, especially in a large network. Direction, interface pairing, and topology version must be preserved. An old or incomplete link map can make a fluent answer more dangerous, which is why [[Network Knowledge Refresh]] is part of the design.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network Copilot Design","Network Knowledge Refresh","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageSt